  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiff",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BAIDA: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: There are two reasons why the State of Maryland has the authority to regulate Virginia and its citizens when they seek to place structures in and withdraw water from the Potomac River."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument next in No. 129 Original, Virginia v. Maryland."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiff",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and it has never relinquished the sovereign authority that its title to the river gives it to regulate what takes place on and over the bed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Do you think the compact covers withdrawals of water by Virginia? I mean, does it directly cover that at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, do you -- do you take the position that Maryland could reject every effort by Virginia to withdraw water from the river?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: So we're talking about -- all we're talking about is property rights here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What provision of the Constitution?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baida",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BAIDA: I think the Due Process Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stuart A. Raphael",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RAPHAEL: No, Your Honor, because we contend that no permit was required in the first instance, and we also challenged that specific permit because the Maryland legislature required that it contain a condition requiring the water authority to put a flow restrictor into the pipeline for the sole purpose, the Maryland legislature said, of allowing Maryland to control growth and development in northern Virginia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0001-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, Maryland has circumvented that requirement by controlling the tap."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Maryland",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Maryland can contend either in the permitting process or independently that any action by a Virginia citizen that -- that it can show causes injury to Maryland shouldn't be allowed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Master ruled that under the compact and the award, Virginia and its citizens have the right to withdraw water and to construct improvements appurtenant to the shore without having to get permission from Maryland."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And what is the source?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Maryland",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Only -- there are only three properties that are taxed by Maryland and those are unique. They're restaurant properties that are sited on property that's -- the fee simple title to which is recorded in Maryland."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, generally riparian owners are own -- have the -- the right to withdraw water subject to the overriding control of the governmental body that controls the -- the lake or the river, whatever it is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Raphael",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RAPHAEL: It is true here. Virginians can withdraw water subject to paramount Federal control and subject to Virginia's control."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: No, it doesn't say as a sovereign. It -- it says Virginia. It does not say as a sovereign."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baida",
      "case_id": "2003-129o",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3e90f2c9119ca8a8c77a3b5ac9ad14aa1d7d46ba750da447c55abc59ce80e17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3e90f2c9119-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Title to -- Virginia has title to low-water mark, but only a right of use beyond that point. It has not an unrestricted right of use. The right of us is subject to governmental authority. The government that gets to regulate it is the government that owns it."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
